package main

// V158 CHECKPOINT-CONTINUOUS CHUNK LOAD: a retry/resume starts from the durable
// unfinished snake lane instead of replaying corner 1 and then diagonally jumping
// across every cache-skipped lane. A failed large-obstacle A* search is negatively
// cached for four seconds so the 50 ms wall-follow stream can keep moving instead
// of spending every frame searching 16000 nodes again. Route travel now times out
// only after it stops making meaningful approach progress.

// V157 EXACT PRE-27 BASE + 20BPS + HIGH-FIRST ONLY: start from the user-confirmed normal pre-27 build, change only the clear-flight stride from 23 to 20 blocks/s, and add a read-only upper-layer residual guard before descending. No chunk-loader, ACK, turn, A*, scan-order, or movement-sync logic is removed.

// V148 NO-MID-PAUSE: fixed 60/s clearing never waits for a saturated acknowledgement window; stale/unconfirmed ACKs are deferred to the mandatory same-lane residual scan instead of stopping or backtracking the forward snake.
// V148 FIXED-60 + EXPANDED CLEAR LIST + LARGE-OBSTACLE PATHFINDER: keep exactly three normal START actions per 50ms work tick; clear bedrock/netherrack plus dirt-family, sand-family (never sandstone), gravel-family and soul sand; preserve every other block and route around large preserved regions with cached 2D flight A* while lava remains avoid-only.

// V147 FLUID-LAYER FIX: preserve solid layer-0 behavior, but track Bedrock/Geyser secondary fluid storage and Extra updates separately so same-Y lava is actually visible to the 5x5x5 and layer-completion scans.

// V147 WALL-FOLLOW + ADAPTIVE + LAVA-LAYER + ONE-SIDE RECOVERY: keep corner-1 snake order, adapt normal START density to real server acceptance, process lava on the current Y layer with a 3-tick authoritative sequence, and never rotate a recovery lane merely because a long backtrack is still making progress.

// V147 STABLE SERVER-CADENCE: forward clear work has priority over acknowledgement retries; enlarge the async confirmation window, never backtrack mid-lane merely because an ACK is delayed, and make failed lava probing non-blocking so one persistent lava cell cannot stall the 50 ms clear stream.

// V147 CORNER-1 FIXED START: every clear_bedrock run physically enters the top-layer first snake corner before work; cached residuals no longer become the task origin.

// V147 CHUNK TRUTH + BATCH UPDATE FIX: retire stale UpdateBlock point overrides whenever a newer full LevelChunk/SubChunk replacement arrives, so temporary air cannot permanently mask server rollback bedrock/netherrack.

// V147 THROUGHPUT TELEMETRY: preserve stable clear behaviour and expose real normal-clear START, server-confirm, retry and observed rollback rates in the live task status.
// V147 STABLE RESIDUAL-FIRST: keep the 20 TPS clear stream at one steady cadence. Do not switch every lane into the slow per-block strict confirmer. A whole Y layer is repaired by the same fast pipeline until two authoritative scans report zero targets. Every task start/resume first searches the selected region for the earliest known remaining target and jumps directly there before continuing normal snake order.
// V147 ONE-PASS CLEAN: preserve the current stable same-layer snake, but identify clear targets by canonical runtime identity (including hashed Bedrock network IDs) and retry an unconfirmed click before it leaves legal reach. This prevents whole patches from being silently skipped or deferred behind the bot.
// V147 SCAN FIX: final verification treats unknown cache cells as unresolved, fully loads every lane before declaring it clean, and never accepts an unloaded chunk as empty.

// V141 SMOOTH AUTHORITY SYNC: keep continuous server-coordinate reconciliation
// without forward/back rewinds, remove correction-driven speed pulsing, throttle
// the 5x5x5 lava scan, and allow clear-bedrock navigation a small X/Z halo while
// all block modifications remain strictly inside the user-selected work bounds.
// Delayed MovePlayer samples are never used as an accepted-position rewind anchor.
// V143 SKIP EMPTY SNAKE: keep V142 smooth movement, but never force travel to lane start/end through already-known empty space. Each lane moves directly toward its next live bedrock/netherrack target; an empty lane is skipped with zero route movement.
// V142 SMOOTH NO-REWIND: active walking/flight ignores normal MovePlayer echoes; only explicit server corrections can change live movement. Clear-bedrock stall recovery stays in-stream and defers unreachable targets instead of stopping/rebuilding.
// V133 FUNCTION-PARITY UI/PROGRESS: preserve the existing V132 Bedrock login,
// clearing, flight and inventory behaviour; add the missing full-function UI,
// real Creator backend and server/task-backed progress reporting only.
// V132 FLYING SINGLE-CLICK CLEAR: clear_bedrock no longer runs the normal
// timed mining lifecycle for bedrock/netherrack. While flying, each reachable
// bedrock/netherrack target gets exactly one left-click START action on the
// normal 20 TPS movement frame; the task advances immediately and lets the
// existing lane verification repair any missed server updates.
// V130 SERVER-PACED SINGLE-FLIGHT CLEAR: clear_bedrock keeps at most one work
// coordinate outstanding, advances immediately after the exact UpdateBlock
// confirmation, drains lava from an in-bounds 5x5x5 cube one coordinate at a
// time, and walks around every preserved solid without changing movement speed.
// 4:11 REQUESTED CLEAR-BEDROCK PATCH (V128 BASE): fixed 50 ms / one-block
// movement, same-height obstacle avoidance, nearby lava packet batches, no
// physical verification backtracking, and separate movement/packet rates.
// V129 40-ROW BURST + LAVA PACKET FIX: keep one legal 20 TPS movement stream,
// but dispatch up to two 3-wide Z rows (six targets) in each 50 ms authoritative
// frame. Clear-bedrock work flight uses a faster dedicated stride, stall recovery
// reacts sooner, and hash-aware lava packets include the server-authoritative mine
// request so lava is removed in the same batched frame instead of pinning movement.
// V128 DIRECT TRUE-SNAKE + 3-WIDE FAST ROWS: clear_bedrock chooses the
// nearest legal snake endpoint instead of entering the region centre first,
// keeps every lane/layer endpoint continuous, and sends all three reachable
// bedrock/netherrack targets in the current row in one 50 ms authoritative frame.
// Server rollbacks repeat the same full-row fast path and never downgrade a lane
// to one-target mining.
// WORK-FLIGHT 20 BLOCKS/SECOND:
// All task flight keeps one legal PlayerAuthInput every 50 ms and advances at
// most 1.00 block per frame. Ordinary work transit, clear-region/explosion,
// placement/mapart and vertical flight therefore share the same 20 blocks/sec
// cap; X/Z diagonal travel remains vector-normalised to that total speed.
// V70 TRANSLATED CHUNK RESOLUTION + INTERPOLATED FLIGHT: when Geyser keeps a
// skeleton column under the active dimension but delivers the usable block data
// under one translated dimension ID, resolve the exact position across the
// same-column snapshots instead of letting the empty skeleton hide it. Task
// flight remains one PlayerAuthInput per 50 ms, with sub-block horizontal and
// vertical strides so other clients see continuous movement instead of nearly
// one-block jumps.
// V69 NATURAL CHUNK RELOAD + SMOOTH ASCENT: restore the last working
// movement-driven Java/Geyser chunk loading path, never send SubChunkRequest for
// clear-bedrock, accept a unique translated-dimension chunk snapshot, and advance
// horizontal/vertical flight independently at the normal 20 TPS cadence.
// V68 DECLARED SUB-CHUNK + UNIFIED FAST MOTION: after exact physical chunk
// entry, wait for that chunk's skeleton/request-mode LevelChunk declaration,
// then request offset 0 exactly once. Task flight, clearing and construction all
// keep a continuous 20 TPS cadence without the old 300 ms placement pause.
// V67 JAVA/GEYSER SAFE STREAM: never emit the SubChunkRequest that stalls this
// Java-backed Geyser connection; physically enter the blocking chunk instead.
// All task flight uses one fast 20TPS pace, work lanes stay 1.75 blocks behind
// and 1-2 blocks above targets, and direct-air placement sends one primary
// UseItemOn packet instead of a six-packet/750ms retry chain.
// V66 GEYSER SUB-CHUNK CENTRE: request vertical chunk data from the live player
// sub-chunk with a target offset, suppress duplicate bursts, and restore the
// original 0.48-block 20TPS flight pace.
// V64 TRUE SNAKE + SMOOTH STREAM FAST AUTO-STANCE: strict row-by-row snake direction, exactly one PlayerAuthInput per 50ms movement tick, temporary correction backoff with automatic speed recovery, +0.5 hover height, and target-only/direct-row chunk streaming.

// V64.10 TRUE-SNAKE FAST: mine while advancing toward each live target; never pre-run a full row before mining. Keeps wall auto-switch and smooth 20TPS flight.
// V59 STRICT-LAYER BURST: continuous 16ms full-range snake flight + same-layer multi-block burst mining. A lower Y layer is never touched until the whole layer above is server-confirmed clear.
// V59 INVENTORY EXACT: dashboard(3).html / 2026-08-22 final backpack baseline is restored byte-for-byte; 4 armour + 2x2 crafting + result + restricted offhand + 3x9 main + 1x9 hotbar + drag/drop/auto-drop remain intact.
// V59 PAUSE/RESUME: paused task state can no longer be overwritten by a late progress update, and stream shutdown sends one neutral hover frame so Descend/Sneak does not stay latched.
// V55 STALL RECOVERY: bounded ordered stream now force-rescans instead of deadlocking on an exhausted acknowledgement.

// V54.3 COMPILE FIX: restores candidate item names required by ordered burst/reliable pipeline.
// V55 STALL RECOVERY + V54.3 SKIN APPLY FIX: active startBot Dialer sends botClientData(bot.ID).

// V54.1 ORDERED-BOUNDS+INVENTORY COMPILE FIX: same V54 behaviour; removes unused nextName/name locals that blocked Go build.
// V54 ORDERED-BOUNDS+INVENTORY: V53 ordered multi-block burst + strict user XYZ flight/work bounds + recovered Codex-complete inventory system.

// V50 ORDERED PIPELINE: strict top-down snake order, one active break target per 20TPS tick,
// short reliable repair bursts only; never permanently downgrade the whole region task.
// Codex inventory recovery source: main_villager_auto_trader_v7_full_form_scroll_read_20260821_1007.go.
// Its v16-inventory-autodrop-theme-fix/icon/resource-pack chain is preserved; newer inventory backend fixes in this file are retained as a superset.

